CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ explicitly instantiated: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
N5008 [temp.explicit]/1, /10: `template int box<char>::put(long);' is an
explicit instantiation definition of a member function template
specialization, its template argument deduced from the function type
([temp.explicit]/2).  The front end declared it as written, a bodiless
non-template member put(long) that hid the member template ("no body for
callee box<char>::put", bin53).  It is now accepted and the
specialization instantiated on use.  libstdc++ instantiates
basic_ostream's _M_insert this way (bits/ostream.tcc).  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
